-- title:
--   Units away from v detected by r-power denominators in R₀
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1$ and the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H = \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$. Let $R_0, R'$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H$, each an order in the sense of the project predicate `IsOrder`: containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $\mathbb H$ over $\mathbb Q$, and finitely generated. Let $r$ be a prime and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $r \in v$, and assume that for every height-one prime $w \neq v$ the local boxes agree, $\mathrm{localBox}\,R'\,w = \mathrm{localBox}\,R_0\,w$, where $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,w$ is the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_w$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb Q_w$. Two conclusions are asserted. First, for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb H$: $x$ lies in `awayUnits R' v`, i.e. in the intersection over all $w \neq v$ of the preimages under the map $u \mapsto u \otimes 1$ of the subgroup generated by the units $u$ of $\mathbb H \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_w$ with $u, u^{-1} \in \mathrm{localBox}\,R'\,w$, if and only if there are $K, K' \in \mathbb N$ with $r^K x \in R_0$ and $r^{K'} x^{-1} \in R_0$. Second, every $y \in R'$ satisfies $r^K y \in R_0$ for some $K \in \mathbb N$.
--
--   This identifies the group of units of $\mathbb H$ integral at all places away from $v$, for an order $R'$ whose local boxes agree with those of a reference order $R_0$ outside $v$, with the group of elements having $r$-power denominators with respect to $R_0$ — the $\{r\}$-unit description of the group acting in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph. It is used in the construction of the coset graph at $v$ and in the rigidification of fake elliptic curves with quaternionic multiplication.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_mem_awayUnits_iff_exists_pow_smul_mem_of_forall_localBox_eq.lean

